# Approval routing for the ISMS.
#
# A merge into main requires review from the approver team listed here. Document
# owners are recorded in frontmatter and remain accountable for content; they
# are not the approval role. Combined with branch protection this records an
# independent approver for the exact merged revision.
#
# Replace the placeholder teams below with real, non-owner approver teams before
# enabling branch protection. Teams avoid approval depending on one person.

# Fallback: anything not matched more specifically
*                       @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director

# Data layer — changes here move the SoA and the risk picture
/data/                  @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director
/data/risks.yml         @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director
/data/soa.yml           @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director

# Automation — a change here can weaken every check
/tools/                 @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director
/.github/               @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director

# Governing documents (clause 4-10)
/docs/en/00-context/    @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director
/docs/de/00-context/    @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director
/docs/en/20-procedures/ @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director
/docs/de/20-procedures/ @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director

# Topic policies — delegate per area once owners are known, e.g.
# /docs/*/10-policies/secure-development-policy.md  @isms-testorg/engineering
/docs/en/10-policies/   @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director
/docs/de/10-policies/   @isms-testorg/dev-managing-director
